All 16 functions from `KernSmooth/R/all.R` have been converted to Python and written to `ablation/conversion_guides/placebo/10/all.R/`, in dependency order (leaves→roots):

1. linbin, rlbin, linbin2D, blkest, cpblock, .onAttach, .onUnload — leaves
2. bkfe, locpoly, sdiag, sstdiag — depend on linbin/rlbin
3. bkde, bkde2D, dpih, dpik — depend on tier 1/2 functions
4. dpill — root, depends on 6 other converted functions

Every function with an internal `.Fortran(...)` external dependency (linbin, rlbin, linbin2D, blkest, cpblock, locpoly, sdiag, sstdiag) had no matching conversion guide, so each was reimplemented natively in NumPy by reading the corresponding Fortran source in `KernSmooth/src/`. Most conversions (bkfe, locpoly, sdiag, sstdiag, bkde, bkde2D, dpih, dpik, dpill) were validated against the actual R `KernSmooth` package via `Rscript` and matched to floating-point precision. No errors occurred during the batch.
